"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under Throws."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ, relative to itself as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when given, is at least 1."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" products","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"laplacianSpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Throws","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE29normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs8smallest9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0G0VyxGSi_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF"